WEBVTT

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.770
An unbearable pressure—the stress—

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.800
is causing something inside his head 
to expand and turn into popcorn.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.400
An Anti-Mysterious Purse.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:19.730
If you put your popcorn in 
here, it won't disappear.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.820
Mom is in the hospital 
because her heart hurts.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.230
She's sad because you won't stop 
making things and playing with them.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.530
It's my fault?

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.240
That's all of them.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:35.930
Huh?

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.610
They disappeared.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.070
Where did the sparkles that 
were inside my head go?

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:52.710
Aona, I enjoy seeing the things you make.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.160
So, why don't you make something?

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.460
It's obvious what you like to do.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.670
What?

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.860
You mean you don't know?

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.410
What is this?

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:17.090
You said you'd keep your promise.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.890
Mom will be sad.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.520
I'm sorry.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:27.960
That's part of the treatment 
I prescribed for him—

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.640
Mind your own business!

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:30.980
What?

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:32.900
Shun, we're leaving.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:40.720
Hey, why is your wife 
actually in the hospital?

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.100
Stay out of my family's business!

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.320
You're grounded.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:19.380
<b>Dr. Ramune
Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:26.470
<b>Episode 8 "Popcorn Head - Part Two"</b>

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:26.680
Aona's still not here?

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.960
Apparently he has a cold.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.410
It's so hot...

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.540
Doctor.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:39.370
Huh?

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:40.800
What is it?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.950
Is there nothing I can do for him?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.190
Of course there is.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:54.740
You've figured out what's causing the 
popcorn and what it really is, haven't you?

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.410
More or less.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:01.450
It comes as naturally to him as breathing.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.550
That's why it's taking him 
so long to figure it out.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.930
Until Aona figures it out,

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:13.770
it's up to you to protect that bag.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.080
I will.

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:22.900
Maybe my concerns were groundless.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:30.850
Shun, I'm going to visit 
Mom in the hospital.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:33.340
Be good and study hard, okay?

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:34.120
Okay.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:41.800
<b>Science Lab</b>

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:42.300
Today we'll be performing 
an experiment using helium.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.740
Okay.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:48.610
Since air is heavier, I expect the helium 
balloon to be pushed to the middle.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:54.120
Hey, you're late.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:54.950
Hey.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.330
Are you feeling better?

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:01.290
Aona, are you sure you're okay?

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.760
Aona, your bag...

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:05.570
Kuropi.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:08.390
<i>You made more popcorn.</i>

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:12.920
Recently I stopped seeing sparkles.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.170
I wonder why.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:17.220
I feel so heavy.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.430
Hey, wait!

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.670
<b>Shiranui General Hospital</b>

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.400
Thank you.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:31.600
Now, then... Let's go check things out.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.210
Hey, no running!

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:33.790
Huh?

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:35.430
Isn't that...

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.310
Kuro? Kuro.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.910
Hey, Kuro-san. Kuropi?

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.610
Kuromame. Kurogoma.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.380
Shorty!

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:47.220
It sounds like you want 
to be hospitalized again.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.160
You idiot, calm down.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:52.160
You're going to visit his mom, right?

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.150
I'll go with you.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:57.380
How are you feeling?

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.670
<b><i>Aona Fuyuno</i></b>

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:01.160
Much better, but it still hurts a little.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.320
I see.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.460
I thought we were going inside.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:08.040
Shh. We'll scout things out first.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.760
I'm sure they'll reveal 
something eventually.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.500
Anyway, I must be getting old.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.270
I can't believe I was hospitalized 
for a strained back.

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:20.570
What?!

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:20.570
Hey!

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:24.140
Oh? You're Shun's classmate.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.410
Hey, you dirty old liar!

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:28.730
No! It's not what it looks like!

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:29.940
Huh? What?

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.900
You said <i>what?!</i>

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.790
You mean Shun thinks it's his 
fault that I'm in the hospital?

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:37.790
Yes.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.530
Honey, why would you lie about that?

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.030
Darling, would you like me 
to get you some pudding?

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:46.670
Don't try to change the subject, old man!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:50.880
But...

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.390
<b>Aona Shun Exhibition
  End of Line</b>

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.250
Get your tickets here.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:58.350
Shun-kun, have you considered 
studying abroad?

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:04.020
I don't want Shun to leave me!

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:09.660
Given Shun's talent, he'd 
surely become famous!

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:12.980
And if he starts working overseas, 
I won't be able to see him anymore!

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:16.650
I couldn't handle that!

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.300
So I was willing to use your hospitalization

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:24.550
to secure a future in which 
I could be with Shun forever!

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:25.770
Oh, my.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:26.920
He's insane.

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:28.140
I'm sorry I'm such an awful father!

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:30.170
Starting now, I'll stay curled 
into a ball forever!

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.340
Honey, raise your head.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:40.640
It certainly would be sad if 
we couldn't see Shun anymore,

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:45.910
but I'm even more excited to see how 
much Shun's talents will blossom.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:51.410
So, instead of picking that 
flower, let's nurture it, okay?

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.460
O-Okay.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.980
And thank you, too.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:01.640
You came all the way here because 
you were worried about Shun, right?

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:05.180
I'm glad he has such a kind friend.

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.540
We're not really friends—

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:11.290
He's a good guy. I hope they'll 
continue being friends.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.730
You shouldn't lie.

00:08:15.730 --> 00:08:20.260
You hung out with him all night and skipped 
class to be here, but <i>I'm</i> the liar here?

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.810
Next time I visit, I'll bring Shun with me.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:31.210
Please do. Also, make sure you 
tell Shun about our <i>real</i> promise.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.750
"Real" promise?

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:36.200
<b>Shiranui General Hospital</b>

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.810
There's something only Shun can do for me.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.500
<i>I see. I get it.</i>

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:13.280
<i>The popcorn is the sparkles inside my head.</i>

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:18.650
<i>That's why I get sad and my heart 
feels heavy when they disappear.</i>

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:24.990
<i>My brain is too cramped for my sparkles.</i>

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:32.930
<i>So...</i>

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:37.340
<i>I'll let them fly away.</i>

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.470
Yeah, yeah...

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.990
What? Shun-kun?

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:31.850
No, he's not here.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:34.600
Huh? He's not at home, either?

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.110
Yes, we'll look for him as well.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:45.620
<i>I was careless.</i>

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:48.370
<i>He hadn't been to class in a while,</i>

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:51.490
<i>but today he showed up partway 
through the school day.</i>

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.870
<i>Meanwhile, his father was at the hospital.</i>

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.870
<i>Why didn't I notice right away?</i>

00:10:58.540 --> 00:10:59.770
<i>Aona...</i>

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:02.630
<i>was running away.</i>

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:18.380
Aona!

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:22.550
Aona. Aona. Aona!

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.190
Kuropi?

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.200
Why are you crying?

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:32.530
What? Am I crying?

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:37.560
Balloons? The ones we used in class?

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:43.210
Aona, where's the bag?

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:47.020
In space, where there's no gravity.

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:53.260
Until Aona figures it out,

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:57.150
it's up to you to protect that bag.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:58.160
I will.

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:00.380
Aona?

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:04.510
He's asleep.

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:08.660
Hey, Shun!

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.910
Shun!

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.430
What's wrong, Shun? Don't die, Shun!

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:21.460
If you die, I won't be able to go on living!

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:23.170
You idiot! Don't shake him!

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:25.860
He produced too much popcorn.

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:28.120
His brain is overburdened.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:31.920
Hey, Kuro. Get the popcorn out of the bag.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.320
I can't.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:37.800
It flew away with the balloons.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:39.070
What?!

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:46.440
I couldn't do anything for him.

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:48.510
Kuro, are these the balloons 
you were talking about?

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.840
Let's see where this thing goes.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:57.460
Since it's flying east, it probably 
hasn't fallen into the sea.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:01.850
I may not be able to calculate its 
path, but I've got my Vision.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:06.040
It's still in the air.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:08.840
Mister, here's the key to the shrine.

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:10.320
Let your son rest and wait in there.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:12.340
Huh? Okay.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:13.960
Hey, Kuro.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:17.800
Pull yourself together. This isn't like you.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:19.680
Aren't you coming to help look?

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:23.830
Right!

00:13:57.010 --> 00:13:58.140
It's around here somewhere.

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:02.890
I'm amazed. I had no idea 
balloons could fly this far.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:08.720
Doctor, your ankle—

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:10.250
Hey, isn't that it?

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.670
We found it!

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:19.150
Dude, can you believe we actually found it?!

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:20.540
We're geniuses!

00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:23.950
Anyway, what are we going to do about this?

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:28.780
Moke-chan's not smart 
enough to untangle that.

00:14:32.290 --> 00:14:33.290
Hey!

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.850
Wait, wait, wait! It's too dangerous!

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:39.520
You idiot! I'll get it, so 
you get down from there!

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:42.520
How are you going to climb with that ankle?

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:47.470
All right! I'll catch you if you fall!

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.430
<i>That would kill us.</i>

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:57.070
<i>But if I fall...</i>

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:01.310
<i>He always does what he says he'll do.</i>

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:07.110
<i>I won't fall, no matter what.</i>

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:11.780
I promise I'll catch you!

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:12.850
Be careful, Kuro!

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:14.410
Whatever you do, don't fall!

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:22.080
It comes as naturally to him as breathing.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.040
<i>Aona, you idiot.</i>

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:26.810
All right! You did it!

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:37.120
<i>You can't breathe without oxygen.</i>

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:52.110
You're awake, Shun. I'm so glad.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:55.120
Are you okay? Can you get up?

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:04.920
Morumoro alien... Samihada alien...

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:07.730
Unyomaro-kun... fuzzy shrimp...

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.730
You mean you don't know?

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:25.630
Oh, right. Shun, about our promise...

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:27.380
Pappy.

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:29.530
I'm sorry.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:34.640
I can't keep our promise.

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:39.490
You and Mommy will be sad.

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:42.400
I know that, but I still 
can't keep our promise.

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:45.220
I meant to throw these away,

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:48.340
but I can't stop thinking about them.

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:53.320
I don't want to stop doing what I love.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:55.360
Shun...

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:58.500
Jeez. Took you long enough 
to figure that out.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:03.300
You freaking airhead.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.050
Kuropi...

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:09.670
How?

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:15.040
How? I sent that up into the 
sky where there's no gravity.

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:19.260
I told you, there's no such thing 
as a place without gravity.

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:26.350
The only one who can make this 
weightless is probably you, Aona.

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:27.730
Yeah.

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:33.670
Thanks for coming back.

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.320
Shun, I'm sorry.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:43.950
I had no idea you were suffering 
so much and I lied to you.

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:46.570
Go ahead and hit me.

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:47.700
You lied?

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:51.460
Mom's in the hospital because 
she strained her back.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.460
It's not your fault.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:18:00.050
And Mom says there's something 
else she wants you to promise us.

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:01.230
What promise?

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:05.210
Anyway, that's that.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:08.230
I see. Got it.

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.000
I don't know what to do, though.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:14.880
Since all the sparkles in 
my head turned into popcorn,

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:17.480
I can't keep my promise with Mommy.

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:19.320
Let me see that bag.

00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:20.250
Huh?

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:22.100
Salt?

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:24.730
I'm using something like 
that to weaken its effects.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.870
Then we do this.

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:31.210
Here. Eat up.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.220
What? I can eat this?

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:39.060
It vanished.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:49.900
Those sparkles have returned to your brain.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:56.890
And you figured out how to keep them 
from leaving your head again, right?

00:18:58.310 --> 00:18:59.120
Yeah.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:07.910
Sorry for turning you 
into popcorn, sparkles.

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:19.030
I'll make all of you before 
you turn into popcorn.

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:30.890
Hey, Mister.

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:37.400
You'll be paying for your son's and 
my apprentice's hospital bills.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:40.000
Okay.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.910
<b>Shiranui General Hospital</b>

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:43.580
Oh, my goodness!

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:44.650
How pretty!

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:50.640
I wanted to fill my hospital room with 
your sparkles so I wouldn't be so lonely.

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:53.550
I'm sure I'll recover in no time now!

00:19:54.030 --> 00:19:58.440
Thank you for keeping your 
promise to me, Shun.

00:19:58.440 --> 00:19:59.920
We have that other boy to thank.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.080
What boy?

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:05.040
You know, your classmate. 
The smallest boy in your class.

00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:10.850
He came all the way here because 
you were feeling down.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.420
Morning.

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:17.110
Kuropi, morning.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:18.050
Good morning.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:24.590
Your hand—

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:25.830
How's your mom?

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:29.570
She was really happy.

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:32.180
She said she'll get better soon.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:33.840
I see.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:35.520
Thanks, Kuropi.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:39.470
I'm glad you're my friend.

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:43.620
Yeah.

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:03.900
<i>That moment...</i>

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:05.780
Hey, Kuro.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.450
Pull yourself together. This isn't like you.

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.500
Aren't you coming to help look?

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.650
<i>I couldn't have done it alone.</i>

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:22.330
Thank you.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:29.690
You're welcome.

00:23:03.490 --> 00:23:05.170
Next right.

00:23:06.120 --> 00:23:08.430
Turn left at the corner.

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:15.450
Akatsuki

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:28.680
